STAGE 21 AUDIT — VERIFIED
The TX-submission action callback is invoked from IOSkywalkTxSubmissionQueue::legacyDequeue and ::listDequeue.
Both call sites load the action pointer from [queue + 0x20] and call it with the action arguments. legacyDequeue then tests EAX; zero means no packets progressed, while nonzero EAX is accumulated and used to advance ring slots. listDequeue adds EAX to its dequeued count and subtracts EAX from outstanding slots.
Conclusion: TX-submission action return value is a packet count, NOT an IOReturn error status. A nonzero kIOReturnNotReady/kIOReturnBadArgument value can be misinterpreted as an enormous packet count.
The separate 3-argument IOSkywalkQueryFreeSpaceHandler at [queue + 0xF0] is not the TX-submission action; Stage20's distinction remains correct.
The Stage21 output's BLOCKED status was a runner classification bug: it searched the list of file paths for the literal METHOD_FILE marker. The 24H32 assembly files were present and have now been inspected.

